<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <!--
    Issues' cross-section surface, carved into its own leaf project because one of its
    consumers is still in Base: CleanupIssuesJob (Humans.Infrastructure/Jobs) purges
    terminal issues nightly, and recurring jobs are named by concrete type in Shell's
    roll-call with no discovery seam yet (design §15.6b). A Contracts/ *folder* inside
    Humans.Issues would therefore make Base reference a section and cycle
    (design §15.5b, memory/architecture/section-project-cycle-fix.md).

    It holds exactly what lives outside the section: the nav-badge count Shell's
    NavBadgesViewComponent renders, the retention call the job drives, and IssueCategory —
    the one Issues enum another section names (Humans.Agent's route_to_issue proposal) and
    which therefore cannot follow the entities into the section's internal Domain/.
    Everything else Issues does — the triage surface, the thread, the list projection, the
    mutation results — has no consumer outside the section and stays internal.

    References Humans.Interfaces only — the bottom of the graph.
  -->

  <ItemGroup>
    <ProjectReference Include="..\..\Humans.Interfaces\Humans.Interfaces.csproj" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
